==============================================================================
(1) IS SMITH STRICTLY STRONGER THAN CAMPBELL?
==============================================================================
  monodromies killed by SMITH but NOT by Campbell (proving strictness):
     d=4  D_4        |G|=8   |stab|=2
  -> containment is STRICT: True
  -> the predicted witness D_4 present: True

==============================================================================
(2) DOES 'monodromy inside A_d' IMPLY GALOIS?  (character-detectability)
==============================================================================
  d=2 : every transitive subgroup of A_d regular? True  
  d=3 : every transitive subgroup of A_d regular? True  
  d=4 : every transitive subgroup of A_d regular? False   counterexamples: A_4
  d=5 : every transitive subgroup of A_d regular? False   counterexamples: D_5, A_5

  -> the discriminant (sign) character detects Galois-ness EXACTLY at d = 3.
     At d >= 4 an even monodromy need not be Galois, so no single quadratic
     character can carry the reduced JC one rung up.

==============================================================================
CROSS-CHECK vs canon (klein-S325: 'd=2 impossible; d=4 allows only A_4/S_4')
==============================================================================
  d=2 allowed monodromies: NONE
  d=4 allowed monodromies: ['A_4', 'S_4']
